  "version": "0.2",
  "source": "manual-seed (2026-05-25), taxonomy normalised 2026-08-12",
  "notes": "Android framework API -> permission/capability metadata for summarize_capabilities. TWO AXES, kept separate so the aggregate Counter stays meaningful: `categories` is ONE axis (domain / behaviour) and no tag may be implied by another, so one call site is never counted twice under two names for the SAME concern -- a second tag is only correct when the API genuinely spans two domains (e.g. WifiManager.getScanResults -> WIFI + LOCATION), and then it does count once in each. `flags` carries the orthogonal, cross-domain concerns a domain tag cannot express (today only IDENTIFIER: the API provably returns a device/user identifier). Facts already stated by the key (IMSI for getSubscriberId, MAC_ADDRESS for getAddress, ...), severity judgements (RISKY) and argument-dependent guesses (POTENTIAL_ANDROID_ID -- resolve_call_args answers that properly) are deliberately NOT tags. Keys must be METHOD descriptors: a field descriptor silently matches nothing (find_call_sites_to resolves methods). The two vocabularies below are the CLOSED sets summarize_capabilities validates `only_categories` against, so a tag that is not here is a loud error instead of a silently empty report; a replacement catalog must declare its own.",
  "category_vocabulary": [
    "ACCOUNTS",
    "BLUETOOTH",
    "CAMERA",
    "CRYPTO",
    "DYNAMIC_LOAD",
    "LOCATION",
    "MICROPHONE",
    "NATIVE_CODE",
    "NETWORK_IO",
    "PACKAGE_INFO",
    "PROCESS_EXEC",
    "REFLECTION",
    "SETTINGS",
    "SMS",
    "STORAGE",
    "TELEPHONY",
    "WEBVIEW",
    "WIFI"
  ],
  "flag_vocabulary": ["IDENTIFIER"],
